  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: efd909a3726f65a42a788984c2369af3, type: 3}
  m_Name: Activity_Greenhouse
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: MarsOutpost.Runtime::MarsOutpost.Core.ActivityDefinition
  id: greenhouse
  displayName: Plant Lab
  tagline: Run a fair red-light trial with seedlings.
  description: Compare red light with a dark control and choose a careful claim.
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  hubOrder: 1
  estimatedMinutes: 2
  requiredForMission: 1
  simulationNote: Inspired by NASA OSDR study OSD-314. Trial signals, lamp power, and science points are invented game values - not NASA measurements or farm predictions.
  sceneName: 03_Greenhouse
  instructionTitle: Set up a fair plant-light trial
  instructionBody: 'The greenhouse has young Arabidopsis seedlings in Mars-like gravity. Give one tray red light and keep the other dark as the control.


    NASA OSDR study OSD-314 compared 6-day-old seedlings in microgravity and Mars-like gravity with red light or darkness. At Mars-like gravity, red light accompanied recovery of cell-growth parameters. The study measured cell growth, cell division, and gene activity - not food yield or oxygen output.


    Set up the trial, compare the simulated signals, then choose the sentence the study can support.'
